Method for Creating new Project Manifests

Status: Accepted

Context:
- A user creates a new Project, which must trigger the creation
  of a Project and ApplicationSet manifest so ArgoCD recognizes
  the project, workflows can be assigned, and test environments
  can be utilized. I must decide whether the Orchestrator uses
  the Kubernetes API to create the manifests or the established
  cluster repository (which would be consistent with bootstrapper).

Decision:
- The Orchestrator will use the Kubernetes API to provision the 
  Project manifests, explicitly rejecting the App-of-Apps GitOps pattern for now.

Other options:
- Utilizing the ArgoCD GitOps route.

Consequences:
- Much faster/easier implementation 
- Highly deterministic and less error prone.
  (relies on etcd optimistic concurrency)

- Not 100% auditable
- Not safe in the case of cluster meltdown/etcd failure
  (Configuration lives purely within k8s)

Justification/Notes:
- While GitOps is the best candidate, there's a lot of things that can go wrong and would need to be handled by the Orchestrator (concurrent branch changes, bad yaml w/o immediate feedback, handling of secrets, need for additional polling)
